            <h1>Latest News</h1>
            <ul>
      <li class="news-item">
        <div class="date">2026-10-10</div>
        <h2>Obituary for Dr. Michael Diepenbroek</h2>
        
                <a href="https://www.pangaea.de/news/obituary-michael-diepenbroek.php">
                
                <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="News item">
                    
        <p>Dr. Michael Diepenbroek died on September 5, 2026. With his passing, the international research data infrastructure community has lost a visionary scientist, builder, and pioneer of the open and sustainable use of scientific data. We deeply miss an inspiring colleague, friend, and mentor whose curiosity, energy, and enthusiasm touched and guided people in countless ways.</p>
        
                </a>
                    <div class="clearfix"></div>
      </li>
        <li class="news-item">
        <div class="date">2026-08-17</div>
        <h2>Event/Campaign related metadata changes finalized</h2>
        
                <a href="https://wiki.pangaea.de/wiki/Event-Campaign-Merge">
                
                <img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="News item">
                    
        <p>To better support the evolving needs of the global research community across all disciplines, we implemented a significant update to our database architecture in the lasts months. Today we deployed the last piece of the transition to our service infrastructure: All deprecated elements from the XML based PANGAEA metadata schema were removed. Starting from today, new and updated datasets will no longer contain &quot;backwards compatibility elements&quot; in the XML-based native PANGAEA metadata. In the following weeks we will also restructure the size information, so our systems better report size of data matrix and binary attachments.</p>
        
                </a>
                    <div class="clearfix"></div>
      </li>
  </ul>
<p>
<span class="glyphicon glyphicon-triangle-right"></span>
<a id="more-news-link" href="/news/">Show all 99 news items...</a>
</p>
